      "content": "The proponents of the Sovereign Resilience Act are driven by a pragmatic understanding of the interconnectedness of the global economy, recognizing that unilateral actions will only exacerbate systemic risks. In contrast, the protectionist faction is driven by a misguided nostalgia for a bygone era of national isolationism, which will ultimately undermine the very stability they claim to seek. The former perspective acknowledges the need for collective action, while the latter prioritizes short-term domestic gains over long-term global prosperity.",
      "source": "target",
